# Shell scripts must stay LF: a CRLF makes the shebang `#!/bin/sh\r` and Linux
# (the Raspberry Pi) then reports "No such file or directory" on exec. This repo is
# edited on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which would otherwise re-introduce CRLF.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The linux/ tree builds and runs on the Pi -- keep its sources LF too so a Windows
# checkout/edit does not flip line endings under the Pi's gcc/systemd.
linux/**/*.c       text eol=lf
linux/**/*.h       text eol=lf
linux/**/Makefile  text eol=lf
linux/**/*.service text eol=lf
linux/**/*.default text eol=lf
